course: dictionary
lesson: 8360
title: Rotor
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A rotor is a part of a machine that turns round and round. You can find the meaning from the clues around the word. «A helicopter's spinning blades are long thin wings going round in a circle» tells you that spinning and going round are what a rotor does.
explain: The word can mean different things, so the context matters. In «With 3 rotors of 26 letters each, Enigma had 26 × 26 × 26 = 17,576 rotor starting positions», rotors are the turning parts inside a machine, not blades. Check by swapping in turning part: «With 3 turning parts of 26 letters each» still makes sense.
explain: A quick check helps you. Ask: what is the rotor doing? Then ask: is it a part, and what kind of machine? In a helicopter it is the blades, in a wind turbine it is the hub with its blades, and in a motor it is the spinning part inside.
fact: A rotor is a part of a machine that turns round and round.
fact: «Rotor blades» are the blades that spin on a helicopter, and the «tail rotor» stops the helicopter from spinning round.
fact: «A drone flies with four or more small rotors spinning at different speeds.»
fact: In a wind turbine, the rotor is the hub with its blades, and the wind turns it to help make electricity.
fact: In science, you can make paper spinners to test rotors and air resistance.
exercise: «A helicopter's spinning blades are long thin wings going round in a circle.» What is the rotor in this sentence? | *The blades that spin round | The fuel tank under the seat | The wings that stay still | The tail that points backwards
exercise: In a wind turbine, what does the wind turn? | The cable on the ground | The tower's shadow | A cloud over the hill | *The rotor, the hub with its blades
exercise: «A drone flies with four or more small rotors spinning at different speeds.» Find and copy one word that means turning round and round. | *spinning | flies | drone | small
test: What does a tail rotor do on a helicopter? | Makes it go faster | *Stops it from spinning round | Makes the rotor blades bigger | Lights up the cabin
test: Which is the rotor in a wind turbine? | The base in the ground | *The hub with its blades that the wind turns | The cable | The tower
exam: What does rotors mean in «With 3 rotors of 26 letters each, Enigma had 26 × 26 × 26 = 17,576 rotor starting positions»? | A spinning top toy | Letters on a keyboard | The tail of a helicopter | *Turning parts inside the machine
